  "step_1": "The decision reason focuses on outcomes with probabilities less than 20%, adjusting their weight upward by 10 percentage points. In this decision problem, both lotteries have outcomes with probabilities of either 50% or 100%, and there are no outcomes with probabilities below 20%. Therefore, the condition for applying the probability weighting (increasing weights for small probabilities) is not met. As a result, the decision reason would not modify any probabilities and would simply use the objective probabilities to evaluate the lotteries. The reason would then compare the weighted sums of outcomes. However, since no outcome qualifies as 'small probability' (<20%), the adjustment has no effect, and the reason reduces to expected value calculation in this case. Thus, the reason can technically be applied, but its distinctive feature (probability weighting for small probabilities) does not come into play.",
